<p>Wall Street economists had expected June industrial production to rise 0.2 percent and estimated that June capacity use would be at a rate of 83.6 percent.</p>
<p>Overall motor vehicle assemblies rose in June. For new cars, the rate was unchanged from May at a rate of 5.8 million a year. But for light trucks the assembly rate rose to 5.8 million in June from 5.4 million in May.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles and parts, June industrial output was up 0.2 percent after a 0.3 percent increase in May.</p>
<p>The Fed noted that continued strength in commercial aircraft and high-technology sectors contributed strongly to June output growth.</p>
<p>During the second quarter, industrial output gained 4.3 percent after a 4.4 percent increase in the first quarter.</p>
